Drop the dead legacy store of gbFactor

The branch for a config file older than version 1.6 sets gbFactor to
zero. The reader then runs the unguarded read of the same key, which
takes the value of the file or the shipped default of minus three.
Nothing reads the field between the two lines, so the assignment reaches
no reader.

The sibling assignments of the block stay live, because the reads of
groupBox and gbLabel sit in the matching else branch.

Drop the assignment. No value changes, and the block now states only
what it still decides.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 7 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
index a87d1bca..dba55b55 100644
--- a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
+++ b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
@@ -1223,7 +1223,6 @@ bool qtcReadConfig(const QString &file, Options *opts, Options *defOpts, bool ch
                      groupBoxLine=readBoolEntry(cfg, "groupBoxLine", true);
                 opts->groupBox=framelessGroupBoxes ? (groupBoxLine ? FRAME_LINE : FRAME_NONE) : FRAME_PLAIN;
                 opts->gbLabel=framelessGroupBoxes ? GB_LBL_BOLD : 0;
-                opts->gbFactor=0;
                 def->focus=FOCUS_LINE;
